#import "src.typ": *

The flight controls hold the #jet.short inside its angle-of-attack and g limits (@flight-controls), and the low-speed warning tone marks the least speed for manoeuvring#afi[paragraph 3.13.2]. In an unusual attitude the reference for the recovery is the helmet's flight symbols#afi[paragraph 4.1.2]. A recovery procedure for a jet that has left controlled flight is not public: open. What #row("AUTO_RECOVERY") does is inferred from its name.

#in-sim[The jet stays controllable at its limit: with the stick fully back it holds about 50° angle of attack and comes back within a few seconds of a full push. There is no deep stall to recover from. *A tone sounds above about 52° angle of attack*, just past the limit. #term("Not modelled"): AUTO RECOVERY (it moves only) and any automatic recovery.]
